# ClickUp Provider

The **ClickUp Terraform Provider** enables platform engineers, DevOps teams, and workspace administrators to manage ClickUp organizations as Infrastructure as Code (IaC). Automate workspace hierarchy, project templates, webhooks, permissions, goals, and chat channels deterministically.

Built natively on the modern [Terraform Plugin Framework](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/plugin/framework) (Protocol v6), the provider supports both ClickUp REST API V2 and ClickUp REST API V3 with plan-time validation and structured error reporting.

## Features

- **Full Workspace Hierarchy**: Automate Spaces, Folders, Lists, Tasks, and Views across your ClickUp teams.
- **Dual API Architecture**: Fast V2 REST client combined with a strongly-typed V3 client for modern endpoints like ClickUp Chat.
- **Workflow Automation & Webhooks**: Configure and manage event-driven ClickUp webhooks with endpoint validation.
- **Access Control & Collaboration**: Provision Team users, Guests, User Groups, and granular permission levels (`read`, `comment`, `edit`, `create`).
- **Time Tracking & Goals**: Track time entries and define OKRs with Goals and Key Results as code.
- **Plan-Time Validation**: Catch invalid URLs, conflicting parameters, and disallowed states during `terraform plan` before touching remote APIs.

## Example Usage

### Provider Configuration

```terraform
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.0"
  required_providers {
    clickup = {
      source  = "rixlhq/clickup"
      version = "~> 0.1"
    }
  }
}

# Configure the ClickUp Provider using an API token
provider "clickup" {
  api_token = var.clickup_api_token
}
```

### Complete Workspace & Project Setup

```terraform
# Query authorized teams (workspaces)
data "clickup_authorized_teams" "current" {}

locals {
  team_id = data.clickup_authorized_teams.current.teams[0].id
}

# Create a Space with project management features enabled
resource "clickup_space" "engineering" {
  team_id  = local.team_id
  name     = "Engineering"
  private  = false
  features = {
    due_dates = {
      enabled               = true
      start_date            = true
      reminders             = true
    }
    time_tracking = {
      enabled = true
    }
    checklists = {
      enabled = true
    }
    custom_fields = {
      enabled = true
    }
  }
}

# Create a Folder within the Space
resource "clickup_folder" "sprints" {
  space_id = clickup_space.engineering.id
  name     = "Sprint Planning"
}

# Create a List inside the Folder
resource "clickup_list" "sprint_backlog" {
  folder_id = clickup_folder.sprints.id
  name      = "Sprint 42"
  content   = "Sprint 42 Backlog and Deliverables"
}

# Provision a Task
resource "clickup_task" "infra_setup" {
  list_id     = clickup_list.sprint_backlog.id
  name        = "Setup Cloud Infrastructure"
  description = "Provision cloud environment and CI/CD pipelines via Terraform"
  priority    = 1 # 1: Urgent, 2: High, 3: Normal, 4: Low
  status      = "to do"
}

# Register a Webhook for task updates
resource "clickup_webhook" "task_events" {
  team_id  = local.team_id
  endpoint = "https://events.example.com/clickup-webhook"
  events   = [
    "taskCreated",
    "taskUpdated",
    "taskDeleted"
  ]
  space_id = clickup_space.engineering.id
}

# Provision a ClickUp Chat Channel (V3 API)
resource "clickup_chat_channel" "dev_ops" {
  workspace_id = tostring(local.team_id)
  name         = "devops-announcements"
  visibility   = "PUBLIC"
}
```

## Authentication & Credentials

Authentication requires a ClickUp Personal API Token.

1. In ClickUp, go to your **Settings** > **Apps** > **API Token**.
2. Click **Generate** to create your personal API token.
3. Export the token in your environment:

```sh
export CLICKUP_API_TOKEN="pk_1234567_abcdef..."
```

Alternatively, supply the token via the `api_token` argument in the provider block.

